    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other files are the base class and the capture util).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline saved the owner but never emitted an audit record. I added an audit step following the project's OfficeFloor conventions:\n\n1. **New function class** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` (in `rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 one public `service` method taking the `@Val Owner`, logging via an `AUDIT`-named SLF4J logger:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   AUDIT.info(\"Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n           owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\n2. **Wired it into** `owners.POST.yml` as an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance. Placing it after `save` guarantees the owner id has been assigned; placing it before `respond` keeps it inside the successful-create path.\n\nThe emitted line \u2014 `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-14` \u2014 contains all three required values (id, customerCode, registrationDate), which is exactly what `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate()` asserts against the captured `AUDIT` logger.",
